From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blong <belohnung@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:00:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Rejoin the MatrixRTC session after the membership manager
 gives up

The membership manager stops after roughly the delayed-leave delay (10s by
default), by which point the homeserver has also removed our membership. A
short homeserver outage (e.g. a node drain) left us connected to the SFU but
invisible to everyone else, with our audio not rendered by the others.

LocalMember now joins again with backoff (1s doubling up to 15s) for up to five
minutes, resetting once the membership reports Connected, and only then reports
the MembershipManagerError. GroupCallView (now CallView) no longer turns the first error into
the connection-lost screen.

Ported to v0.24.0 from largelanguagemeowing/cinny 365deb7c. Upstream
added a StickyEventsRequiredError branch to the same GroupCallView
handler since 0.20.1; that branch stays (retrying cannot fix a
homeserver without sticky events, so LocalMember does not retry it), and
only the ConnectionLostError fallback goes. The test that pinned that
fallback is replaced by one asserting the call stays up.

Rebased onto v0.26.1: GroupCallView became CallView (and its test
CallView.test.tsx, where upstream's ConnectionLostError fallback and
Reconnect tests are replaced the same way), joinMatrixRTC now takes the
resolved delayed-leave timings (61eeb817), so the rejoin passes the same
timings as the first join, and LocalMember takes localTransport instead
of localTransport$. Upstream still turns the first MembershipManagerError
into Connection lost.
